OL,3,GNEWSAWoman who escaped rapist abuser
OL,4,Aboyfriend 'can breathe again'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA victim of coercive control who was
OL,7,Fsubjected to physical and sexual abuse
OL,8,Fwhile pregnant and after having her
OL,9,Fbaby has said she can now "breathe
OL,10,Fagain" after seeing her abuser jailed.
OL,12,FNicole, from Manchester, said she lived
OL,13,Fin permanent fear and felt like a
OL,14,F"hostage" at the hands of 22-year-old
OL,15,FElliot Allen Bulman.
OL,17,FShe said she was afraid for the life of
OL,18,Fher unborn child, adding: "All I kept
OL,19,Fthinking was the impact that it would
OL,20,Fhave on the baby if he hit me in the
OL,21,Fback or stomach."
